{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>And these are the kings, etc.</b> They were eight, and corresponding to them Jacob rose up and abolished the kingship of Esau in their days — these are they: Saul and Ish-boshet, David and Solomon, Rehoboam, Abijah, Asa, Jehoshaphat. And in the days of Joram his son it is written: ״בְּיָמָיו פָּשַׁע אֱדוֹם מִתַּחַת יַד יְהוּדָה וַיַּמְלִיכוּ עֲלֵיהֶם מֶלֶךְ״ (II Kings 8), and in the days of Saul it is written: ״וּמֶלֶךְ אֵין בֶּאֱדוֹם נִצָּב מֶלֶךְ״ (I Kings 22)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:02:18.842309449Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}